This repository contains two kinds of material under two licences.

1. The software (everything outside content/ and public/content/: the converter, the
   logic engine, the web app and the API) is released under the MIT License below.

2. The book. content/source/ is the unmodified LaTeX source of "forall x: Calgary. An
   Introduction to Formal Logic" by P. D. Magnus, Tim Button, J. Robert Loftis, Robert
   Trueman, Aaron Thomas-Bolduc and Richard Zach, licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0); the licence text is in
   content/source/LICENSE.md and the credits are in the book's preface. content/build/ and
   public/content/ are derived from that source (converted to JSON, solutions placed next to
   their exercises, a handful of bracket and citation slips corrected, see docs/ERRATA.md) and
   remain under CC BY 4.0. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by the authors.

Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts at run time (STIX Two Text and Source Sans 3, both under the
SIL Open Font License). KaTeX is used under the MIT License.

